# Announce that a formula is true, publicly.
#
# This is the counterpart of the problem expert's `set predicate`, and it is
# not the same operation. Setting a predicate changes what is true. Announcing
# changes what is *known*: the model is restricted to the worlds where the
# formula holds, so every agent that could not previously tell those worlds
# apart from the others now can, and knows that the others know it too.
#
# It is how an operator, or a sensor outside the plan, tells the system
# something all the agents witnessed. Knowledge that reaches only one agent is
# not a public announcement and cannot be expressed this way; that needs an
# event model, which is what an action is.
string formula
---
bool success
string error

# The state after the announcement. A public announcement can only remove
# worlds, so num_worlds never grows.
uint32 num_worlds
uint32 num_designated
